      "content": "the phase relationship thing actually makes a lot of sense. i was looking at the building's smart integration specs and it's all interconnected—everything is on a single centralized control loop. it feels like it's too deliberate to be just a coincidence. if someone *did* want to influence the level of tension in a room, how would they actually go about layering those frequencies without it being obvious to a casual observer? i'm trying to figure out if this is something i can actually shield myself from in my unit.",
